<title>AUSTRIA: Raiffeisen arranges convertible zloty bond.</title>
<headline>Raiffeisen arranges convertible zloty bond.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austria's Raiffeisen Zentralbank Oesterreich AG said on Tuesday it had arranged the first-ever convertible bond issue for a Polish borrower.</p>
<p>The bank said the 7.5 million zloty issue had been arranged as a private placement for construction group KPBP Bick. The subscription period started today, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Bick would use the proceeds for further acquisitions and to finance the modernisation of its equipment.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 53112 274</p>
</text>
